       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Love Language Quiz FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a love language quiz?\", \"a\": \"A love language quiz is a short set of questions that shows which love language a person's answers favor, such as Quality Time or Acts of Service. The idea comes from a 1992 nonfiction book by Baptist pastor Gary Chapman, which outlines five general ways that romantic partners express and experience love.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a love language quiz?\", \"a\": \"Describe the quiz in a prompt, and Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> writes the questions, a result screen for each language, and the table that saves every result. Ask for a follow-up in the same prompt or a later one, such as an email to you when someone finishes. Then share the link.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should each result in a 5 love languages quiz tell the person?\", \"a\": \"It should name the leading language and show what it looks like in a normal week. Chapman's book includes questions to help readers identify both their own and their partner's primary and secondary love languages. Show the runner-up too. Close with two small things to try, like a phone-free dinner for Quality Time.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I offer a free love language quiz on my own website?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent's free tier covers building and publishing. Keep the result screen free of sign-up walls. The setup behind it, where each option points to one result, is the same one that runs a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/style'>style quiz</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should my free 5 love languages quiz ask for an email before the result?\", \"a\": \"No, show the result first. A visitor asked for an email before seeing anything has no reason to trust the quiz yet. Put an optional email field under the result, with a plain reason to give it, such as two ideas a week for their language. On Emergent, every address lands in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should a five love languages quiz have?\", \"a\": \"Eight is a good number. With one option per language in each question, 8 questions give every language 8 chances to come out ahead, and a person on a phone can finish in one sitting. Past 10, the questions start to sound alike. The quiz on this page uses 8.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does a love language quiz decide which result to show?\", \"a\": \"It counts. Each option points to one language, and the language picked most often becomes the result. No answer is right or wrong, unlike a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/vocabulary'>vocabulary quiz</a>, which scores answers against a key. Decide ahead of time how a tie breaks, for example by showing both languages.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where do the five results in a love language quiz come from?\", \"a\": \"They come from The Five Love Languages, a 1992 nonfiction book by Gary Chapman. He theorizes that people tend to naturally give love in the way that they prefer to receive love. That is why a good quiz asks both how someone likes to be cared for and how they show care.\"}, {\"q\": \"How accurate are love language quiz results?\", \"a\": \"Treat them as a starting point. Scientific studies on the validity of love languages have yielded mixed or inconclusive results, and a 2023 review found that existing research does not confirm that individuals reliably have a preferred love language. Say so in one line on the result screen, and frame each result as a leaning.\"}, {\"q\": \"How can a coach use a love language quiz to find new clients?\", \"a\": \"Put the quiz where prospects already read, like a newsletter or podcast show notes, and end each result with one offer. If the offer is a free first session, send that click to a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/free-trial'>free trial landing page</a> that explains the session and books it. The app records which result each new client came from, in a database you own.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6af44d7f042b2574421e295b",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Personality Quiz Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a personality quiz?\", \"a\": \"A personality quiz is a short set of questions where each answer adds a point to one of several result types, and the type with the most points becomes the result. The quiz on this page asks eight questions about a free day and names one of four types.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a personality quiz?\", \"a\": \"Write down the result types and what each one should lead to, then describe the quiz in a prompt. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> writes the questions and the scoring, and builds the result screens. Add a tiebreak rule or a weekly results email with a follow-up prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many results should a personality type quiz have?\", \"a\": \"Four or five results suit a personality type quiz of eight to ten questions. Each type then appears in every question, and you can still write descriptions that do not overlap. Past six, two types start to share options, and the results get harder to tell apart.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I make a free personality quiz for my website?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing a free personality quiz. The same setup works for a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/style'>style quiz</a>, where the result names a fashion style instead of a personality type.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I pick animals for an animal personality quiz?\", \"a\": \"Write the personality types first, then give each one an animal your audience already pictures in that role, and test the pairings on five people. In an animal personality quiz, every option still maps to a type. The animal is the name and the image on the result screen.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a personality quiz maker save from each person?\", \"a\": \"Keep the result, each answer picked, and any email the person entered. The answers matter as much as the result: they show which question decides the most results. A personality quiz maker that writes to a database you own lets you read those rows yourself, and Emergent builds it that way.\"}, {\"q\": \"How is a personality quiz scored?\", \"a\": \"Each option adds a point to one result type, and whichever type leads after the last question is the result. Nothing is right or wrong. A knowledge quiz such as a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/vocabulary'>vocabulary quiz</a> works the other way: one option per question is correct, and the score counts the correct answers.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should a personality quiz have?\", \"a\": \"Eight to ten questions is a workable length. With fewer, each type gets only a handful of points, and one stray answer can swing the result. Emergent builds the quiz with one question per screen when you ask, which keeps a ten-question run short on a phone.\"}, {\"q\": \"What happens when two personality quiz results tie?\", \"a\": \"You set the rule. The quiz on this page gives a tie to the result listed first. Another option is a tiebreak question that appears only when two types are level. Pick one rule before launch, then test it with a run that splits your answers evenly.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where should I put a personality quiz on my website?\", \"a\": \"Put it where the result changes what the visitor sees next: a product page, a booking form, or the newsletter sign-up. A software company can place one on a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/free-trial'>free trial landing page</a> and open the trial with a setup guide matched to each result.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6ad0a185b930ffc59a752ed3",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Poll Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What are some funny poll questions?\", \"a\": \"Here are five funny poll questions that pick on no one. Is a hot dog a sandwich? Pineapple on pizza: yes or no? Socks with sandals: crime or comfort? Would you rather lose your keys or your phone charger? Is cereal a soup? Before you post one, try your funniest poll questions on two friends and keep the ones that get an answer straight away.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create poll questions?\", \"a\": \"Write one question with two to five answers, decide who may vote and when the poll closes, then share the link. In Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a>, you describe the poll in a sentence, and Emergent builds a voting page you can share by link. A follow-up prompt changes the question, the answers, or the closing time.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some fun questions to ask in a group poll?\", \"a\": \"Ask questions every member can answer without a debate. Pizza or tacos for the next get-together? Which decade had the best music? Beach week or mountain week? Early bird or night owl? Group poll questions like these are quick to answer, and some of them settle a real plan, such as where to eat next time.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some good poll questions?\", \"a\": \"Good poll questions ask about one thing and offer answers people can pick at a glance. Which day works best for the team lunch? Which of these four outings gets your vote? Was today's meeting too long or about right? Multiple choice poll questions like these end with a clear count. When you need details, such as where a repair is needed, use a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/work-order'>work order form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some fun poll questions I can ask my friends?\", \"a\": \"Try these fun poll questions with friends. Would you rather explore space or the deep sea? What is the best road trip snack? Which movie deserves a rewatch? Cats or dogs? Save anything that splits the group, like money or politics, for a real conversation, and keep your poll questions for fun light.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some poll questions?\", \"a\": \"Poll questions come in a few types. This or that: Mountains or ocean? Multiple choice: Which board game goes on the shelf next? Rating: Rate this week's all-hands, 1 for wasted time and 5 for time well spent. Open: What name fits the new conference room? For a busy channel, this or that poll questions make the easiest poll of the day questions.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are good would you rather poll questions?\", \"a\": \"Good would you rather poll questions offer two choices that are equally tempting or equally annoying. Would you rather give up coffee or dessert for a month? Would you rather always arrive 10 minutes early or 10 minutes late? Would you rather work a week from a beach or from a cabin? Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing a poll like this.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where should a website place opinion poll questions?\", \"a\": \"Place an opinion poll where readers have formed a view: at the end of an article, beside the topic it asks about, or on the page people see after they finish a task. Ask one question per poll. Show the results only after a vote, and keep the poll away from the content people came to read.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which poll questions are allowed in a work chat?\", \"a\": \"Questions anyone can answer without sharing something private are fine: lunch spots, weekend plans, and this-or-that choices. Aim funny poll questions for work at shared work life, such as Monday mornings or the printer, never at a coworker. Leave out politics, religion, health, and pay. Keep fun poll questions for work optional.\"}, {\"q\": \"How can a business make poll questions profitable?\", \"a\": \"Tie each poll to a decision that costs or earns money. Ask customers which flavor to stock next or which delivery day suits them, act on the winner, and compare sales before and after. Build the poll app with Emergent, and it can send each vote to a tool you already use, such as your CRM, through its API.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6af6c0bb52c80a5b19d1ef73",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Skin Type Quiz Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a skin type quiz?\", \"a\": \"A skin type quiz is a short run of questions about how skin feels bare and behaves through the day, ending in a named type. Dermatology usually classifies skin by five types: dry, oily, normal, combination, or sensitive. The quiz on this page asks 8 questions and sorts answers into the first four.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a skin type quiz?\", \"a\": \"Describe it to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> in one prompt: the types you want, the questions to ask, and what each result screen shows. Emergent builds the quiz and the logic behind it, and the app saves every finished quiz with its answers. Name any change in a later prompt, from a question's wording to the products on a result screen.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a skincare quiz ask before it recommends products?\", \"a\": \"Ask how skin feels an hour after washing, where shine shows by midday, how pores look, and how a new cream sits after a week. Add one question on scent if you carry fragrance-free lines, and keep the whole skincare quiz under 10 questions so people finish it at a counter or on a bus.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a Fitzpatrick skin type quiz the same as the one on this page?\", \"a\": \"No. The Fitzpatrick skin type is a classification first developed in 1975 by Thomas Fitzpatrick, MD, with six phototypes going from light to dark. The quiz here sorts by oil and comfort instead, the way a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/style'>style quiz</a> sorts by taste, and its takers land on a routine rather than a phototype.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should a find your skin type quiz ask?\", \"a\": \"Six to 10, if each question separates at least two types. One bare-face question, a midday shine check, pores, a season change, and a blotting test cover the ground without losing anyone. Emergent sets no response caps, and a short quiz can sit on every page of your site at once.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a Baumann skin type quiz based on?\", \"a\": \"The Baumann system is composed of 4 spectra, starting with dry to oily and sensitive to resistant, which cross into 16 skin types. Build on it only if you can write 16 distinct result screens; a four-type quiz keeps every result backed by products you carry.\"}, {\"q\": \"How is a skin type quiz different from seeing a dermatologist?\", \"a\": \"A skin type quiz reads what a person reports; a dermatologist examines the skin itself. Skin type can also change over the course of a life; treat any result as a snapshot. Keep result copy descriptive rather than clinical: a quiz can place someone the way a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/vocabulary'>vocabulary quiz</a> places a reading level, and it should never diagnose.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I run a skin type quiz for free?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing. Paid plans add full code export to a GitHub repository you own, which matters once a developer takes the quiz over.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does a skin types quiz tell combination from normal?\", \"a\": \"By where the shine sits. A T-zone that turns shiny by midday while the cheeks stay comfortable points to combination; no shine and no tightness anywhere points to normal. In a matching quiz each option adds a point to one type; write the shine options so the two types never blur.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should the result screen of a what's my skin type quiz offer next?\", \"a\": \"Give the taker somewhere to go: the routine for that type, a link to each product in it, and one opt-in for a follow-up email. A sample offer or a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/free-trial'>free trial landing page</a> converts takers who want proof before a full-size purchase. The app stores each result beside its answers, and the follow-up can quote exactly what someone said.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6af44d7f042b2574421e295d",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Spirit Animal Quiz Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a spirit animal quiz?\", \"a\": \"A spirit animal quiz is a short quiz that matches your answers to one animal and describes what your choices lean toward. Each option points to an animal, and the animal with the most picks is your result. The term borrows from spirit animals, which UW-Madison's housing guide describes as spiritual guides that take the form of animals often viewed as sacred in tribal cultures.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a spirit animal quiz?\", \"a\": \"Name the animals, the number of questions, and where each result should lead, and Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> writes the quiz, a page for each animal, and the table that stores every result. Change any question with a follow-up prompt, then publish the link.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I make a free spirit animal quiz for my website?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing. Describe your animals and questions in one prompt and publish the quiz. Link to it from any page of your site. Each finished quiz is saved to a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make an online spirit animal quiz result feel accurate?\", \"a\": \"Build each result from the options that lead to it. If the otter's options are swimming, a crowded table, and a game night, the otter result should name those habits back to the reader. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/style'>style quiz</a> works the same way, with clothes and colors in place of animals.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should the result screen of a what's my spirit animal quiz show?\", \"a\": \"Show the animal's name and a photo first, then two lines on what the answers leaned toward. Under that, add one next step, like the trail where that animal lives or a book list, and a share link that opens the same result page for a friend.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I keep one animal from winning most of the time in my spirit animal quiz?\", \"a\": \"Count the results after the first 100 plays. With 4 animals, each should land near 25. If one takes 40 or more, move one of its options to the animal with the fewest results. On Emergent, a follow-up prompt changes the mapping, and the next visitor plays the new version.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a spirit animal quiz teach kids facts about animals?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if the result pages carry the facts and you check each one against a zoo or wildlife group's own page. The quiz itself sorts preferences and has no right answers. For questions with one correct option and a score, use the format of a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/vocabulary'>vocabulary quiz</a> instead, with score bands for the result.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is it respectful to call my quiz a spirit animal quiz?\", \"a\": \"Not to every reader: some people object to the term. UW-Madison's inclusive language guide says non-native people appropriate the term to relate themselves to an animal. A title such as 'What is your animal match?' keeps the spirit animal quiz format without the term, and the quiz on this page uses one.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I run my animal spirit quiz on a tablet at an event?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Ask for one question per screen and a restart button on the result page, which sends the next visitor back to question 1. There is no cap on responses in an Emergent app, and every play at a busy event is saved with its animal and the time it finished.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where should I share my spirit animal quiz?\", \"a\": \"Share it where your visitors already look: the newsletter, a social post, a QR code on a sign by an exhibit, or the homepage. For a product sign-up, a 4-question version can sit above the form on a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/free-trial'>free trial landing page</a>. Track which link brought each play in the results table.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     }
    ]
   }
